      "question": [
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68539",
          "text": "<p>A sequential circuit has three D flip-flops $A, B, C$ and one input $X$. The circuit is described by the following input equations:</p>\n\n<p>$$D_A = (B\\bar C + \\bar BC ) X + (BC + \\bar B \\bar C) \\bar X , \\\\D_B = A , \\\\D_C = B$$</p>\n\n<p>What is the next state for the circuit for $X=0$ when present state $A, B ,C$&nbsp; is $0, 0, 0$?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>0 1 0</li>\n    <li>1 0 0</li>\n    <li>0 0 0</li>\n    <li>0 0 1</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go-digital-logic-1,digital-logic,circuit-output",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68541",
          "text": "<p>Find the minimum sum of products form of the below Logic function :</p>\n\n<p>$$F(A,B,C,D) = \\sum m(0,2,8,10,15) + \\sum d(3,11,12,14)$$</p>\n\n<p>where $m$ and $d$ are min-terms and don’t care conditions respectively.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$AC +\\bar BC \\bar D +B\\bar C $</li>\n    <li>$\\bar B&nbsp; \\bar D&nbsp; + AC$</li>\n    <li>$\\bar AC +BC+\\bar B\\bar C \\bar D$</li>\n    <li>$B\\bar C\\bar D + \\bar BA + CA$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,min-sum-of-products-form",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68549",
          "text": "<p>The advantage of Synchronous Sequential circuits over Asynchronous Sequential circuits is :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>\n    <p>Faster operation</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <p>Easy to avoid problems due to Hazards</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <p>Lower hardware requirement</p>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <p>None</p>\n    </li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,digital-circuits",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68561",
          "text": "<p>A set of Boolean connectives is known as functionally complete if all Boolean functions can be Synthesized using those. Which of the following sets of connectives is not functionally complete ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>EX-NOR</li>\n    <li>implication, negation</li>\n    <li>OR, negation</li>\n    <li>NAND</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,functional-completeness",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68578",
          "text": "<p>Which function does not implement the Karnaugh Map given below?</p>\n\n<table cellpadding=\"7\" style=\"width:171px; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">wz</th>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\">00</th>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\">01</th>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\">11</th>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\">10</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">xy</th>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">00</th>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>x</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">01</th>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>x</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">11</th>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>1</p>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <th scope=\"row\">10</th>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>x</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n            <p>0</p>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$(w+x)y$</li>\n    <li>$xy + yw$</li>\n    <li>$(w+x) (\\bar w + y) (\\bar x + y)$</li>\n    <li>All of the above implement the given Karnaugh&nbsp;Map</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,k-map",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68695",
          "text": "<p>The minimum number of Flip-Flops required to construct a binary Modulo $n$&nbsp;counter is ________</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$n$</li>\n    <li>$n-1$</li>\n    <li>$2^n – 1$</li>\n    <li>$\\lceil \\log_2 n \\rceil$</li>\n</ol>\n\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,flip-flop,digital-counter",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68706",
          "text": "<p>The following expression was to be realized using 2-input AND and OR gates, but by mistake all 2-input AND gates were taken as 2-input NAND gates,</p>\n\n<p>$$(a.b).c + (\\bar a.c).d + (\\bar b.c).d + a.d$$</p>\n\n<p>What is the function finally realized ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$\\bar a + \\bar b + \\bar c + \\bar d$</li>\n    <li>$\\bar a + b + \\bar c + \\bar d$</li>\n    <li>$\\bar a + \\bar b + c + \\bar d$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,circuit-output",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68711",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following sets of components are sufficient to implement any arbitrary Boolean function (assume external 0/1 is available):</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>XOR gates, NOT gates</li>\n    <li>2 to 1 multiplexors</li>\n    <li>AND gates, OR gates</li>\n    <li>Three input gates that output $(A.B) + C$ where $A,B,C$ are inputs</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68712",
          "text": "<p>Reduce this Boolean Expression to one literal</p>\n\n<p>$$\\bar W X( \\bar Z +\\bar YZ ) + X( W+\\bar WYZ)$$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>$W$</li>\n    <li>$Z$</li>\n    <li>$X$</li>\n    <li>$Y$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,boolean-algebra",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68714",
          "text": "<p>Total number of full and half-adders require to add 32 bit numbers is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>16 half adders , 16 full adders</li>\n    <li>1 half-adders , 31 full-adders</li>\n    <li>32 half-adders, 0 full-adders</li>\n    <li>16 half-adders, 31 full-adders</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,adder",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68716",
          "text": "<p>In 2's complement addition, Overflow</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>is flagged whenever there is carry from sign bit addition</li>\n    <li>can not occur when a positive value is added to a negative value</li>\n    <li>is flagged when the carries from sign bit and previous bit match</li>\n    <li>none of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,number-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68724",
          "text": "<p>The addition of 4 bits two complement binary numbers $1101$ and $0100$ results in</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>0001 and an overflow</li>\n    <li>1001 and no overflow</li>\n    <li>0001 and no overflow</li>\n    <li>1001 and an overflow</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,number-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68728",
          "text": "<p>The output of a gated&nbsp;<em>S-R</em>&nbsp;flip-flop changes only if the:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>flip-flop is set</li>\n    <li>control input data has changed</li>\n    <li>flip-flop is reset</li>\n    <li>input data has no change</li>\n</ol>\n\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,flip-flop",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68732",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is equivalent expression to $A \\oplus B \\oplus C$ :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$(A+B+C)(\\bar A+\\bar B+\\bar C ) $</li>\n    <li>$( A+B+C) (\\bar A +\\bar B +C)$</li>\n    <li>$ABC + \\bar A(B \\oplus C ) + \\bar B (A \\oplus C )$</li>\n    <li>None</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,boolean-algebra",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68767",
          "text": "<p>The conversion $(E7C.B)_{16}$ to octal is equal to</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>$( 8483.9)_8$</li>\n    <li>$(6894.4)_8$</li>\n    <li>$(8124.5)_8$</li>\n    <li>$(7174.54)_8$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,number-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68773",
          "text": "Determine the Radix $r$\n\n$$(BEE)_r = (2699)_{10}$$",
