        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68775",
          "text": "<p>All digital circuits can be realized using only</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Ex-OR gates</li>\n    <li>AND, OR gates</li>\n    <li>Half-adders</li>\n    <li>OR gates</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,digital-circuits,functional-completeness,combinational-circuit",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68777",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following operations is commutative but not associative ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>AND</li>\n    <li>OR</li>\n    <li>NAND</li>\n    <li>EXOR</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68778",
          "text": "<p>The number 3 in 2’s complement representation is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\n    <li>00000011</li>\n    <li>11111101</li>\n    <li>11111100</li>\n    <li>01111100</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,number-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "68779",
          "text": "<p>Zero has only one representation in</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Sign magnitude</li>\n    <li>1's complement</li>\n    <li>2's complement</li>\n    <li>Both 1's complement and 2's complement</li>\n</ol>\n\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "digital-logic,go-digital-logic-1,number-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        }
